            {
                "entry_id": "5a54fd3b-275a-3215-9e2f-a380c742d532",
                "word": "fructification",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "457f04eb-ed52-40f2-90cb-9973516f3e6f",
                        "entry_id": "5a54fd3b-275a-3215-9e2f-a380c742d532",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "fructifications"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3d625d90-a630-3f67-9caa-fa46123405fa",
                        "entry_id": "5a54fd3b-275a-3215-9e2f-a380c742d532",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of forming or producing fruit; the act of fructifying, or rendering productive of fruit; fecundation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1860f63-62b9-4012-bf55-800e07b67b37",
                                "sense_id": "3d625d90-a630-3f67-9caa-fa46123405fa",
                                "text": "In nature, the wild hop is usually shadowed during its growing period by bushes and trees, and it is only those aboveground parts which are intensively illuminated which pass into fructification period."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9dc681de-a8f8-41e2-ae42-3e074cbe9ece",
                                "sense_id": "3d625d90-a630-3f67-9caa-fa46123405fa",
                                "text": "Lucuma salicifolia (canistal) and Micropholis mexicana (wild apricot) are the most infested fruit species. They have a very short fructification period."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53f1f329-9154-4301-a8d6-2de430d43566",
                                "sense_id": "3d625d90-a630-3f67-9caa-fa46123405fa",
                                "text": "Studying the duration of the flowering-fructification period among interspecific first-generation back-cross progenies of African species showed that this trait is positively correlated (r=0.78) with 100-seed weight and caffeine content."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7dc42e99-45b7-336a-8558-d5c508aac273",
                        "entry_id": "5a54fd3b-275a-3215-9e2f-a380c742d532",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The collective organs by which a plant produces its fruit, or seeds, or reproductive spores."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a54ec0c6-00f3-4100-a221-d7e8a3d4a727",
                                "sense_id": "7dc42e99-45b7-336a-8558-d5c508aac273",
                                "text": "The fructification is liable to become very convex in age."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ea8546d-4c73-4a15-a1c2-a4783579360d",
                                "sense_id": "7dc42e99-45b7-336a-8558-d5c508aac273",
                                "text": "The essence of the fructification consists in the flower and the fruit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f5c138a-49b6-4f2c-a2d7-e8fe081e227c",
                                "sense_id": "7dc42e99-45b7-336a-8558-d5c508aac273",
                                "text": "Postheterotopic transformations played a great role in the evolution of fructifications. The formation of specialized seed-like sporophylls in the Lepidocarpaceae, of strobilar fructifications in the Noeggerathiales, of various capsules and other seed-bearing organs of many gymnosperms belong here."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
